    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For natural stone, especially in a high-traffic environment like a law firm, it's crucial to use cleaning products and sealants that are gentle yet effective. A pH-neutral stone cleaner is essential to prevent any potential damage to the stone's surface. Look for products specifically designed for natural stone, as they will be formulated to clean without stripping the stone of its natural oils.\n\nWhen it comes to sealants, a penetrating sealer is often recommended for natural stone. These sealants penetrate the stone's pores, providing protection without altering the stone's appearance. They are less likely to cause discoloration or damage compared to surface sealants. Reapply penetrating sealants every 6-12 months, depending on the stone type and the level of foot traffic.\n\nFor daily cleaning, a soft, damp cloth with a mild detergent can be used to wipe down the stone surface. Avoid using abrasive materials or harsh chemicals, as they can cause scratches and damage the stone's finish. Regular maintenance, including prompt cleaning of any spills and stains, will help preserve the stone's beauty and integrity over time.",
